experiment seeds-v2  —  80 trials  —  corpus v2
  The same sixteen models as all-v2, across five seeds. This exists because every stored run in the repository before it was seed 0, which means the leaderboard — and the claim that nine of sixteen models score below a popularity baseline — rested on a single draw of the random number generator.
The question is not whether the individual numbers move. It is whether the *ranking* moves, because the ranking is what every statement about these models actually asserts. A model whose rank swings by five places between seeds is not "seventh best"; it is unresolved, and saying otherwise is the same error as quoting an absolute delta across two different test sets.
Seeds are named rather than counted. "Five seeds" is not reproducible.
Note the {seed} and {split} placeholders below. Written literally as svd-ppmi-recipe-holdout-s0, a blend would consume seed 0's parents at every seed, and the sweep would report five identical blend rows while appearing to measure variance. That failure is silent, which is why the templating exists.


